Error [jet.BuildProbeFailed]: Build actions run only in the native sandbox, and none is available here: bubblewrap (`bwrap`) is not available on PATH; Jet's pinned bubblewrap `jet-bwrap-x86_64-linux` is not in the Hangar (`{scratch}/jetpack/hangar/tools/0a0c6389f605169e916aa9b9f424fc1128fc318a539948986cdc639cb183107a/bwrap`) or beside jet; fetching it failed: network disabled by JETPACK_DENY_NETWORK, so https://example.invalid/jet-bwrap-x86_64-linux cannot be downloaded
 Why: Every build action and probe runs in a bubblewrap sandbox, never outside one. Jet uses the `bwrap` on PATH first, because a host that lets only profiled programs create user namespaces (Ubuntu's AppArmor profile for /usr/bin/bwrap) allows only its own copy; if that is missing or fails its probe, Jet uses its own hash-pinned bubblewrap, fetched into the Hangar on first need. Neither is usable here.
 Fix: Install bubblewrap (`bwrap`) with user namespaces enabled, or let jet fetch its pinned bubblewrap (online, or with `JET_BWRAP_URL` naming a copy); Jet never runs a build action outside the sandbox
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E3505
